<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the hardened runtime (tools/package_app.sh with DEVELOPER_ID set, or HARDENED=1).

  Deliberately empty: nothing the app does at run time needs a hardened-runtime exception.
  * Metal shaders are compiled at run time (MTLDevice.makeLibrary(source:)) by the system's
    out-of-process Metal compiler; the app maps no writable+executable memory, so no
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory.
  * libopenmpt and its dependencies are embedded in Contents/Frameworks and signed with the same
    identity as the app, so library validation passes (no disable-library-validation).
  * The app is not sandboxed (no com.apple.security.app-sandbox): reading the CD image or game
    folder the user picks, and writing ~/Library/Application Support/EpicPinballHD, need no
    entitlement. Game controllers (GameController framework) and audio output need none either.
  * No get-task-allow (notarization rejects it) and no DYLD_* environment variables.
  See docs/enhanced/frontend.md "Packaging" for how this was checked.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
